title ALES194 — Lotus's reverb_predelay: the reverb's WHEN knob, the silent gap before the reverberant tail — reverberate wet, then shift the wet onset later within the span
prompt Continue the recursion loop on the ALES / Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve the design round, make progress, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think With the wet/dry pair complete for mono and stereo (ALES192 · ALES193), the reverb has WHICH room and HOW MUCH. The one axis left is WHEN — the pre-delay, the short silent gap before the reverberant tail begins, what sits the room a hair behind the dry rather than smearing over its onset. On a real console it is the single knob that separates a voice from its own reverb and keeps a busy mix legible. By Lindy-first crux-first this is the highest-Lindy tractable move: a genuinely new expressive axis (time, not level or bank) and a clean composition of proven pieces.
think The shape: validate the clock, convert the span with the SAME clock.samples_for reverb_preset uses (DurationTooLong forwarded), validate range (BadRange) BEFORE any write, convert predelay_ms through the same clock and refuse BadPredelay if it exceeds count, run ALES190's reverb_preset over the span (the wet, in place, unchanged), snapshot the wet into a bounded stack buffer, then rewrite the span shifted right by predelay: out[i] = 0 for i < predelay, else wet[i - predelay]. This invents NO new audio arithmetic — the pre-delay is a bounded REINDEX of the proven wet, so no value is recomputed or can wrap, and the gap is filled with true zeros; the last predelay samples of tail fall off the span end, an honest bounded truncation.
think Five laws, each provable: the ZERO-DELAY EDGE (predelay = 0 equals reverb_preset over the span byte for byte — no gap is exactly the un-delayed reverb); the FULL-DELAY EDGE (predelay = count shifts the whole wet off the end, the span all zeros); the SHIFT IS EXACT (a mid pre-delay puts zeros in front and the wet shifted by exactly predelay after, byte for byte against the un-delayed wet run side by side, and genuinely differs from it); SILENCE STAYS SILENCE; the FAULTS FORWARD (a pre-delay past the span BadPredelay, a span past the clip DurationTooLong, an out-of-range span BadRange, the clip untouched). This is a WET-DOMAIN pre-delay — combined with the dry through ALES192's wet/dry mix it is the classic console pre-delay, a later rung.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal pass — no RED to book. TAME bans clean, width exit 0, ALES190 preset re-run GREEN beside it. The pre-delay is a named duration in milliseconds, so it means the same gap at any sample rate; the gap true zeros, no wrap possible. Purely local: one clip, a validated clock, ALES190's fixed banks, a bounded stack snapshot, siloed to lotus/; no socket, network, keys, funds, device, or speaker — no custody gate reached, a self-approved design round.
loom witness=ales_reverb_predelay_witness result=green rooms=3 clip_samples=1024 predelay_mid=16 snapshot_max=4096 preset_rerun=green reds_fixed=0
